# BeanLog — Cursor Rules & LLM Context

## Project Overview

BeanLog is a zero-cost, local-first Progressive Web App (PWA) + native mobile app for specialty coffee analytics.
It ships as a **single codebase** that runs on web, iOS, and Android via **Capacitor**.

Two main features:
1. **Analysis** — Computer vision (OpenCV.js / WASM) to analyze bean size, roast level, and grind distribution via a printable calibration target.
2. **Logging** — Brew journal backed by Supabase (auth + Postgres + RLS) **or local storage (guest mode)**. Users log beans, grinders, and brews with SCA flavor wheel notes. Guest users store everything in `localStorage` and can migrate to Supabase on signup.

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| **Frontend** | React 18, TypeScript (strict), Vite 5, Tailwind CSS 3, Lucide Icons |
| **PWA** | `vite-plugin-pwa` for offline web capability |
| **Native shell** | Capacitor 8 (wraps the Vite build in iOS/Android WebView) |
| **Native plugins** | `@capacitor/camera`, `@capacitor/haptics`, `@capacitor/app`, `@capacitor/status-bar` |
| **Backend** | Supabase (Auth, Postgres with Row Level Security) |
| **Charts** | `chart.js` + `react-chartjs-2` |
| **CV** | OpenCV.js (WASM) loaded in a Web Worker (`src/workers/cv.worker.ts`) |
| **i18n** | Custom lightweight system (`src/i18n/`) — English (`en-us`) and Korean (`ko-kr`) |

